## 4. Exactly What Goes Where

### Placement Matrix

| Component | Where It Goes | Why There |
|---|---|---|
| `LogEvent.java` DTO | `omnicharge-common` | Shared by producers (all services) AND consumer (logging-service) |
| `LoggingConstants.java` | `omnicharge-common` | Queue/exchange names referenced by all |
| `LogEventPublisher.java` | `omnicharge-common` | Reusable bean auto-configured in every service |
| `FallbackLogWriter.java` | `omnicharge-common` | Fallback file writer when RabbitMQ is down |
| Micrometer Tracing deps | `omnicharge-common` pom.xml | Inherited by all services |
| Prometheus registry dep | `omnicharge-common` pom.xml | Inherited by all services |
| Zipkin, Prometheus, Actuator properties | `config-server/config/application.properties` | Global — one place, all services inherit |
| `logging-service.properties` | `config-server/config/` | DB config for the new service |
| Swagger dep (`springdoc`) | Each service's own [pom.xml](file:///c:/Users/vishnu%20vardhan%20reddy/Downloads/OmniCharge/api-gateway/pom.xml) | MVC vs WebFlux variant differs |
| [OpenApiConfig.java](file:///c:/Users/vishnu%20vardhan%20reddy/Downloads/OmniCharge/omnicharge-common/src/main/java/com/omnicharge/common/config/OpenApiConfig.java) | Each service individually | Different title/description per service |
| `logback-spring.xml` | **NOT NEEDED** in business services | Terminal stays untouched; log capture is via code |
| Log file writing logic | `logging-service` only | Centralized — that's the whole point |
| RabbitMQ logging exchange/queue | `logging-service` RabbitMQConfig | Consumer declares its own queue |
| System.out cleanup | `api-gateway` + `user-service` | Fix only the 2 files with System.out |
| `@Slf4j` on GlobalExceptionHandler | `omnicharge-common` | So server errors are logged |

### What Does NOT Change

| Unchanged | Reason |
|---|---|
| Terminal/console log output | User explicitly requested this stays |
| Existing `log.info/error/warn` calls (100+) | They continue on console; we capture them in parallel |
| Existing RabbitMQ Saga queues | Logging uses a **separate exchange** (`omnicharge.logging.exchange`) |
| Redis CQRS read model | Not touched |
| Any business logic | Zero impact |

