## 7. Observability Stack Setup

### Zipkin (Distributed Tracing)
```bash
docker run -d -p 9411:9411 --name zipkin openzipkin/zipkin
```
- Auto-configured via Micrometer Tracing deps + config properties
- Each service sends trace spans automatically — zero code changes
- View at `http://localhost:9411`

### Prometheus (Metrics Scraping)
```bash
docker run -d -p 9090:9090 --name prometheus -v prometheus.yml:/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml prom/prometheus
```
`prometheus.yml`:
```yaml
scrape_configs:
  - job_name: 'omnicharge'
    metrics_path: '/actuator/prometheus'
    scrape_interval: 15s
    static_configs:
      - targets:
        - 'host.docker.internal:8080'   # gateway
        - 'host.docker.internal:8081'   # user
        - 'host.docker.internal:8082'   # operator
        - 'host.docker.internal:8083'   # recharge
        - 'host.docker.internal:8084'   # payment
        - 'host.docker.internal:8085'   # notification
        - 'host.docker.internal:8086'   # logging
```

### Grafana (Dashboards)
```bash
docker run -d -p 3000:3000 --name grafana grafana/grafana
```
- Add Prometheus as data source → `http://host.docker.internal:9090`
- Import Spring Boot dashboard (ID: `12900`) for instant JVM/HTTP metrics
- View at `http://localhost:3000` (admin/admin)

